{title: Call On Me In Trouble}
{subtitle: Psalms 50:15}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 125}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Cm7] [F7] | [Dm7] [Gm7] |
| [Cm7] [F7] | [Bb] [Gm7] | [Cm7] [F7] | [Dm7] [Gm7] |
| [Cm7] [F7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F7]The [Bb]world and all that [Cm7]fills it is [F7]mine
[Dm7]I do not [Gm7]need your [Cm7]flesh or wine
[F7]Do [Bb]I eat the [Gm7]flesh of bulls [Cm7]or drink
The blood [F7]of goats [Dm7]that you [Gm7]think
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Offer [Cm7]God [Bb]a sacrifice of [D7]praise
And fulfill your [Gm7]vows in grace
Then [Cm7]call on me in [Bb]the day of trou[D7]ble
I will deliver [Gm7]you
[Eb]And you will honor me [Cm7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F7]But to the wicked [Bb]God [Bb]says clearly
What right [Cm7]have you [F7]to speak
[Dm7]To [Gm7]recite [Cm7]my statutes [F7]on [Bb]your lips
While [Gm7]you [Cm7]do not keep
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Of[F7]fer [Dm7]God [Gm7]a sacri[Cm7]fice [Bb]of praise
And ful[D7]fill your vows in [Gm7]grace
Then call [Eb]on me in the [Bb]day of trou[D7]ble
I will deliver [Gm7]you
[Eb]And you will honor me [Cm7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F7]You hate discipline [Bb]and [Eb]cast my words be[F7]hind
You [Bb]approve [F/A]the thief [Gm7]and [Cm7]join the sin
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Offer God a sacrifice [F7]of praise
[Bb]And fulfill your [D7]vows in grace
Then [Gm7]call on me [Eb]in the day of [Bb]trouble
I will [D7]deliver [Gm7]you
[Eb]And you will honor me [Cm7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F7]Call on me in the [Bb]day of trouble
[D7]I will deliver [Gm7]you
{end_of_verse}

